ree with a marked test, `kitlib.red_mark.landing_refusal`, has one caller: the integrator's refresh. The coordinator lands every lane in this repo by hand (recipes §3), and partial closes end the same way (recipes §8). That route squashes with `git merge --squash` and runs only the smoke bar, never a refresh. No hook or declared check step reads the mark either.\n\n**It is reachable under PROCESS.md §6.**\n- The hand squash is this repo's documented way to land, not a contrived sequence.\n- The lane's own procedure text now puts strict marks on every tests-first commit, and it promises a marked test is \"never landed\".\n- A mark survives to landing in two ordinary ways: a code commit that leaves one marked test unfixed, or a partial close that keeps the tests-first commit.\n- When that happens, a red test lands on trunk reading as a pass. That is the failure SN-008 rules out. Every later loop lane's refresh would then be refused for a file it never touched.\n\n**Why FIX rather than the other rulings:**\n- **Not DISMISS:** the path is real, reachable and in scope.\n- **Not SUCCESSOR:** the brief forbids it for a fail-open path.\n- **Not ESCALATE:** the fix is small and sits in text this lane already edited. Recipes §3 already runs named checks on the staged squash before the landing commit, so one more step there closes the gap.\n\nThe fix: add a recipes §3 step that runs `kitlib.red_mark.landing_refusal` on the staged squash and resets the squash if it refuses. Then reword the coordinator-cycle sentence \"a refresh refused for a mark…\" so it covers that landing check too.\n\nTwo alternatives don't work here:\n- **The filed one-landing row:** moving the coordinator's landings onto the merge slot is the structural answer. But it isn't this lane's, and waiting for it leaves the lane's new text untrue in the meantime.\n- **A commit-hook step:** marked tests are legitimately present on lane commits between the tests-first and code commits, so a check on every commit would refuse them.","ttft_ms":27011,"type":"result","duration_ms":233008,"uuid":"1b315d52-0903-48c5-b825-411eb6d8a72a","ttft_stream_ms":18938,"time_to_request_ms":189,"first_content_frame_ms":18938,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":9055,"cacheReadInputTokens":3619338,"cacheCreationInputTokens":529413,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":5.140335599999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5145,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":529413,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}]
